                <h3 class="font-bold text-fg">From sensor readings to an early warning</h3>
                <p class="text-muted">Each HVAC node reads current with an INA219 and temperature with a MAX6675, then sends the values to the ESP32 gateway over UART. Every 2 seconds, the gateway adds its own vibration measurements and compares the readings with the learned baseline of that unit. Then it runs a small neural network on the chip: 259 parameters, about 1 KB, written in plain C. The gateway posts the results to a local dashboard that shows health, trends, and the likely cause of a warning.</p>
                <p class="text-muted">SentinelBox learns a separate baseline for each unit from about 90 seconds of normal operation. After that, the status changes only when 3 of the last 5 readings look abnormal, so one spike does not trigger an alert.</p>
